---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import Stage from "../../components/Stage.astro";
---
<Base title="Alert: info, success, warning, danger" description="iVOLT alert: info, success, warning and danger messages with title, body and actions, using role=status or role=alert. CSS only.">
  <article class="docs-prose">
    <h1>Alert</h1>
    <p>A message the user should notice. Use <code>role="status"</code> for informative or success messages and <code>role="alert"</code> only for urgent ones that need immediate announcement. No JavaScript: to dismiss, remove the node.</p>
    <p class="docs-meta"><strong>CSS:</strong> <code>css/components/alert.css</code> (in <code>ivolt.css</code>).</p>
    <Stage primary name="alert/variants" title="Four tones, one shape" />

    <Section title="Anatomy" num={1}>
      <p><code>iv-alert</code> (<code>--info</code> default, <code>--success --warning --danger</code>) with optional <code>iv-alert__icon</code> (<code>aria-hidden</code>), <code>iv-alert__title</code>, <code>iv-alert__body</code> and <code>iv-alert__actions</code>.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Common mistakes" num={2}>
      <ul><li><code>role="alert"</code> on every message: screen readers interrupt the user each time.</li><li>Alerts rendered on page load for content that is not an alert.</li></ul>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Class index" num={3}>
      <p>Parts and modifiers of this family that the examples above do not show. The full list per stylesheet lives in the <a href="/reference">reference</a>.</p>
      <div class="docs-scroller docs-class-index">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>iv-alert--success</code></td><td>Success tone: the icon and the rule take the success colour.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>iv-alert--warning</code></td><td>Warning tone.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>iv-alert--danger</code></td><td>Danger tone; pair it with a text that names the problem, never colour alone.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </Section>
  </article>
</Base>
